{color:#36b37e}Dear Luis,{color}



{color:#36b37e}Please may I instruct your team to advise on some specific aspects of the Lease Agreement you have reviewed?{color}



{color:#36b37e}*Clause 3.3 (Term).*{color}

{color:#36b37e}The current wording says: {color}

{color:#36b37e}_‘After the first five years of the term of the Lease, without having been terminated by the Tenant under the terms of the preceding paragraph, the Lease will remain in force until the end of the ten (10) year term, being then automatically renewed for equal and successive periods of 5 (five) years, unless the Landlord or the Tenant terminates it or opposes its renewal under the terms of the following paragraph.’_{color}


{color:#36b37e}Our business colleagues would like to be able to terminate the Agreement at some point after the fifth year and before the tenth year of the duration. We believe that the Landlord may object to a termination right at any time for Bolt after the fifth year, therefore, could you please{color}

