Hi Jana, Maria,

please see responses to questions 2-6 below {color:#36b37e}in green{color}:

Q2: Do users need to opt-in for their calls to be recorded? {color:#36b37e}No, but they need to be informed that the recording is taking place. Before each call there should automated message informing that: (a) the call is being recorded; (b) data is processed by Bolt Operations OÜ which acts as a data controller; (c) further information on how we handle and secure personal data can be found at our website - {color}[https://bolt.eu/en/legal/|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/]. 

Q3: In what format does this consent have to be asked? {color:#36b37e}As above- no consent needed, but before each call there should be automated message that the conversation is being recorded. We will be relying on different legal basis for recording those calls (legitimate interest).{color}

Q4: How would the user needs to give their consent (voice, press a button etc.)? {color:#36b37e}As above- no consent needed. If the end user doesn’t want to be recorded, then they should end the call and choose other communication method.{color}

Q5: How long can we store the recordings for? {color:#36b37e}There isn’t specific retention period that is set out in applicable legislation, but general rule apply that we shouldn’t keep personal data longer than it is necessary for specific purpose. I’d usually recommend to align the retention period with the limitation period for consumer claims (2 years of limitation period + additional 2 months to secure edge-cases where the claim is made by the end of the limitation period).{color}

Q6: Are there any other issues we should be aware of? {color:#36b37e}Maria will provide general legal overview on that, but on a privacy front specifically, using legitimate interest as a legal basis require us to document legal assessment on that. I will take care of that, but please provide all expected use-cases in relation to this data. I’d expect that that would be mainly defending against any potential claims and quality assurance, but do you foresee any additional purposes of processing here?{color}

